{"calculus_ref":"stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md","clause_relations":[{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:current-boundary-effect","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:executive-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:hard-stop","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Current-boundary effect is the Executive's determination that a finding blocks the current promotion boundary, requires narrowing, or may remain an explicit residual. The Executive then applies exactly one existing disposition. A hard stop or a falsified mandatory claim cannot be waived by lowering priority. An observation outside the exact claim boundary cannot open another review round because it carries a severe label.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:boundary-effect-precedes-exactly-one-disposition"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"candidate_ready -> satisfied; refused -> falsified; incomplete -> indeterminate; re_entry_requested -> out_of_frame or invalid_basis.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:maps-to","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:construction-availability-maps-to-core"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-disposition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"accept, local_repair, re_enter and reject are what the decision owner does with an assessed candidate; a disposition consumes a core result and is not one.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-disposition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:candidate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Assessment of a candidate returns one of four semantic dispositions: accept when the candidate closes its declared cone and preserves every affected governing relation; local_repair when implementation or proof is locally defective while the governing relation remains coherent; re_enter when the governing outcome, a requirement, an identity, a lifecycle, an authority, a public contract or the accepted design must change; reject when the candidate violates a governing relation or leaves an undisposed competing truth path. Global correctness means conserving every global relation affected by the bounded action; it does not require proving the whole product inside every local action. Repeated rejection against one unchanged boundary requires reassessment of the frame altitude, the causal cone, the common components, the design-versus-code placement and the authority sufficiency; the method sets no rejection-count threshold, mandatory review-round count or review state machine, and prohibits repeating an unchanged failed construction relation as if iteration alone could close it.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P5, P4b, P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:dispositions-are-selected-by-their-conditions"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:exact-candidate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:candidate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"An exact candidate is the subject identity that transition evidence and assessment traceability require. Where generic method qualification applies its construction result is frozen before material reference exposure; elsewhere the review subject is stabilised through an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claimed assessment. No new lifecycle state named frozen is created.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:exact-candidate-is-a-stabilised-subject-identity"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:executive-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:candidate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"An actor occupying the Executive frame modifies no candidate, Product or worktree bytes and performs no implementation effect, however small, test-only, reversible or obvious. Mutation requires a separately activated Worker or Writer relation carrying the exact operation grant, subject and write territory; a same-actor role transition is explicit and recorded before the effect. Recording or delegating after an Executive edit cannot authorise it retroactively.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:executive-mutates-nothing"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:drift-lock","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-invalid-basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-out-of-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"On a failed lock: changed Product meaning requires re-entry; a stale or substituted basis is invalid_basis; missing material scope is out_of_frame; missing operation authority refuses the activation or the effect; an unresolved mandatory conflict prevents a satisfied conjunction. The Executive repairs none of these by making its own frame larger.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P5, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:failed-drift-lock-maps-to-its-result"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:drift-lock","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:executive-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Before activation and before disposition the Executive revalidates five locks. Outcome lock: the selected Goal, Product outcome, boundary and lawful re-entry class, the current MVP or release mandate, and the triage policy are unchanged. Basis lock: the subject, authority, dependency, configuration, topology, evidence, time and candidate coordinates are exact and current. Product-role lock: the mutable Source Project, Product Definition, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact and dependent Product identities stay distinct, and every Development Product role stays bound to its exact underlying Install. Authority lock: the semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance and publication owners and grants are unchanged. Coverage-and-return lock: every material evaluation and interaction is closed or an explicit residual, and every consumed result followed its declared return relation.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P6, P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:five-drift-locks-before-activation-and-disposition"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:product-testing-frame-set","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:testing-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The ordinary configuration holds four distinct frames: user acceptance evaluates the Product outcome from the user's supported frame; end to end evaluates the complete runnable causal realisation of that outcome; integration evaluates one material composition boundary and its interaction population; unit evaluates one module-owned law. They add no role, stage, authority or testing hierarchy; the fan-out assigns claims to evidence. A broader frame cannot make a module-owned law true, and any number of narrower green frames cannot establish an unevaluated Product composition or user outcome. A label such as UAT, E2E, integration or unit has no assurance value without the corresponding frame declaration.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P4a, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:product-testing-frame-set-assigns-claims-not-authority"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:current-boundary-effect","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:hard-stop","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Consumed condition -> required Executive constraint: (1) a valid falsification of a mandatory claim governed by a non-waivable hard stop -> the current promotion boundary blocks, whatever the assigned priority or decision cutoff; (2) a valid finding below the Product-owned decision cutoff, with no hard stop -> no block follows mechanically; the Product-owned policy is applied and any accepted residual is kept explicitly; (3) an observation outside the exact evaluated claim -> bounded repricing or re-entry input; it creates no claim-relative block and no further review round by its severity label; (4) an unsupported or materially incomplete technical assessment -> a capable evaluation is reactivated, or indeterminate is kept; Reviewer evidence is not rewritten.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:promotion-constraint-projection"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-disposition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-ambiguity-outcome","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-profile-closure","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A declared refinement answers a different question, keeps its own vocabulary and declares a total mapping to the core; no refinement adds a core member.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:severity","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:priority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:current-boundary-effect","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Severity grades the consequence if the finding manifests. Priority orders the response relative to the complete Product outcome, likelihood and exposure, the current MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies, cost of delay and available capacity. The Reviewer grades severity; the Executive assigns priority. The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis binds the severity scale, the priority scale, the current-boundary decision cutoff and the non-waivable hard stops; this profile imposes no universal numeric scale. Severity, priority, the frame result and the current-boundary effect are four distinct values; none of them alone makes a finding release-blocking.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P1, P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:severity-priority-result-and-boundary-effect-are-four-values"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:work-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:exact-candidate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:product-testing-frame-set","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"For candidate_ready, the Executive verifies the exact subject and decides whether independent assessment is required by EVALUATION section 3, ACTIVATION section 1, EVALUATION section 7 (method qualification), Product, release, risk or the admitted work contract. Green aggregate status cannot satisfy this step when a required user-acceptance, end-to-end, integration, unit or negative-path result is missing, bound to another subject, or contradicted by a material frame result.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6; ASSURANCE section 10","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:testing-evidence-stays-claim-bound","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-4-candidate-ready-decides-independent-assessment"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:work-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:executive-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"For refused, incomplete or re_entry_requested, the Executive verifies the exact basis and applies the existing authority relation; it records the applicable disposition, or reactivates work only where current authority already permits that action. None of these variants is accepted progress because work occurred.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-4-non-candidate-variants-are-not-progress"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:self-review","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:executive-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"When independent review is not required, the Executive consumes the exact candidate, the Worker's self-review, the transition evidence and any mandatory specialist results, and applies the disposition within its decision envelope. Self-review stays Worker evidence; the disposition does not relabel it as independent.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-5a-self-review-stays-worker-evidence"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:assessor","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:exact-candidate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"When independent review is required, the Executive activates the Reviewer with: the exact candidate and governing basis; the exact claim, composition boundary, population, scope and exclusions; the applicable method and project authority; the required evidence and the ordinary assurance path; the required user-acceptance, end-to-end, integration, unit, combinatorial and negative-path frame results with their exact claims and populations; the Product-selected severity scale and the exact affected Product claims; the Reviewer's capability and independence envelope; and invalidation and stop conditions.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-5b-reviewer-activation-contents"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:review-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:assessor","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:technical-triage","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The Reviewer returns one closed evaluation containing: frame and activation identity; the exact subject, basis, claim, scope, exclusions and evaluated population; the Reviewer actor and the independence conditions; the evidence and the ordinary assurance path acquired; the core result; findings, counterexamples and adjacent observations; for each finding, where supportable, the technical-triage fields; invalidation conditions and, where applicable, the re-entry owner. The Reviewer returns to the Executive, not to the Worker, and does not edit the candidate, direct the repair or authorise continuation.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-6-reviewer-returns-one-closed-evaluation-to-the-executive"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:executive-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-disposition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:checkpoint","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:priority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The Executive verifies that every consumed result is still bound to the current subject and basis, revalidates the complete Product view and the current MVP or release mandate, applies any declared result conjunction, assigns priority, records the effect on the current promotion boundary, and acts on exactly one disposition within its grant: accept, local_repair, re_enter or reject. ACTIVATION sections 3 and 5 own each disposition, the exact accepted checkpoint and the next already-authorised bounded action. A repair creates a new candidate, and an affected review is reactivated against it. Acceptance does not widen the Product outcome or authorise an unselected successor.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P5, P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-7-executive-disposes-exactly-once-and-checkpoints"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:severity","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:priority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:hard-stop","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Severity neither selects priority mechanically nor blocks promotion. Priority neither erases severity nor waives a hard stop. The Executive decides blocking from the exact affected claim, the current mandate, the applicable hard stops and the Product-owned cutoff policy. An unsupported technical assessment returns through a new or refined activation rather than being silently rewritten.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-7-severity-neither-selects-priority-nor-blocks"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:technical-triage","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:finding","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:assessor","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Technical triage is the Reviewer's assessment of one finding against the exact evaluated claim and basis. Where admissible evidence and the actor's capability envelope support it, it records: the affected claim and the observed failure; severity on the Product-selected severity scale; causal assessment and confidence; blast radius and the affected users, paths or relations; an available workaround or containment; repair complexity, regression risk and material dependencies; residual uncertainty and the evidence that would reduce it. Missing causal or repair evidence stays explicit; where the missing relation can change the evaluation the Reviewer returns indeterminate or out_of_frame pressure, does not invent precision and does not send work sideways to the Worker.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:technical-triage-records-supportable-finding-fields"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:product-testing-frame-set","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"One execution may provide several bound results. A supported user scenario may supply user-acceptance evidence for the outcome, end-to-end evidence for the runnable causal path, integration evidence for selected seams and unit counterexamples for a module-owned algebra. Those claims stay distinct and combine only through declared REFERENCE_FRAME §6 relations. The default proof responsibilities are: user acceptance proves the outcome from the user's supported frame; end to end proves the complete authoritative runnable Product path; integration proves material participant composition; and unit proves module-owned laws, with evidence size and strategy proportional to their internal combinatorial complexity. Integration and unit results cannot stand in for either broader claim. When the Product claim requires all of them, a conflict or a missing result stays visible to the decision owner's disposition and cannot be hidden by aggregate green status.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4a, P6, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:testing-evidence-stays-claim-bound"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:testing-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:authoritative-product-path","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A test file, suite, runner, fixture, scenario label, coverage percentage or actor does not become a testing frame by existing. A testing frame's authority is bounded by the claim actually exercised; test count, assertion count, source coverage, runtime duration and framework category do not widen it. Producing an expected output through a bypass, an obsolete executor, a test-only seam, an undeclared fallback or a competing authority falsifies path conformance even when the output value is equal.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P1, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:testing-frame-authority-is-bounded-by-the-claim"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:work-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:computed-classification","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The result references the current computed classification, supporting evidence, residual judgments and original rulings through their existing carriers; it does not reconstruct unchanged C/J/O at each handoff. The consumer checks applicability and concrete invalidators; changed evidence revises only the affected results, preserving originals and supported surviving claims.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:work-result-references-existing-classification"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:work-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"It exists only after a successful Worker activation. An activation_refusal (REFERENCE_FRAME §5) returns to the assigning authority or declared result carrier and creates neither a Worker activation nor a Worker result. candidate_ready (with satisfied): an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available; refused (with falsified): lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; incomplete (with indeterminate): the valid activation produced no candidate because admissible evidence or bounded execution cannot yet decide or complete the relation; and re_entry_requested (with out_of_frame or invalid_basis): a material decision lies outside Worker authority, or the activated basis can no longer support the work. The mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation. Payload wording, stop timing or actor preference cannot select another variant.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P5, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:construction-availability-maps-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:work-result-variants-map-totally-to-core"}],"closure":{"clauses":["urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:boundary-effect-precedes-exactly-one-disposition","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:construction-availability-maps-to-core","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:dispositions-are-selected-by-their-conditions","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:exact-candidate-is-a-stabilised-subject-identity","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:executive-mutates-nothing","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:failed-drift-lock-maps-to-its-result","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:five-drift-locks-before-activation-and-disposition","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:product-testing-frame-set-assigns-claims-not-authority","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:promotion-constraint-projection","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:severity-priority-result-and-boundary-effect-are-four-values","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-4-candidate-ready-decides-indepe